# Architecture

## Specifications:

- Laravel 12
- PHP 8.3 FPM
- MySQL 8.0
- Redis 8.10.2
- Nginx 1.31.6

## Key Directories

These are under `app/` directory, which follow `Clean Architecture` guidelines.

- `Console/`:  Folders/Files related to the creation of custom Laravel commands.
- `Application/`: Use cases and application ports. One `{Name}UsecaseInterface` and `{Name}Usecase` per domain, under `Application/{Domain}/`. This layer may depend on `App\Domain`, itself, `App\Repositories`, `App\Models`, and vendor classes. It must not depend on `App\Http` or `App\Infrastructure`.
- `Domain/`: Entities, value objects, enums, and domain exceptions. This layer may depend on itself and vendor classes. It must not depend on other `App` layers.
- `Http/`: Folders/Files related to the HTTP service. Controllers, Middleware, Requests and Resources are managed here.
- `Infrastructure/`: Folders/Files related to external services, such as Media Storage (S3, Mega, Cloud Storage), APIs, etc.
- `Models/`: Folders/Files related to the creation of Eloquent Models
- `OpenApi/`: Files related to OpenAPI specification in the project.
- `Providers/`: Files related to Laravel Providers.
- `Repositories/`: One repository interface and one implementation per domain. Implementations use Eloquent models. Search card repositories stay separate from the aggregate repositories.

## Other Directories

These sit at the project root, outside `app/`.

- `bootstrap/`: Files related to application bootstrap (`app.php`, `providers.php`) and the framework cache.
- `config/`: Files related to application configuration (database, cache, auth, queue, services, and similar).
- `database/`: Folders/Files related to migrations, factories, seeders, and import data.
- `public/`: Web server document root. Holds the front controller (`index.php`).
- `resources/`: Folders/Files related to frontend assets and Blade views.
- `routes/`: Files related to HTTP and console route definitions.
- `schemas/`: OpenAPI component schemas referenced by the API specification.
- `storage/`: Runtime files such as logs, framework cache, sessions, and compiled views.
- `tests/`: Feature and unit tests.
- `.github/`: CI workflow definitions.
- `.cursor/`: Cursor rules for this repository.

## Layer rules

Enforced by `phparkitect.php` (`composer check:architecture`).

- Controllers depend only on a use-case interface. They keep HTTP validation, status codes, and API resources. They do not call repositories or Eloquent.
- Use cases type-hint repository interfaces, not concrete repositories. They return the same models, `PaginatedResult`, `MapResult`, or null that the controller needs.
- Each domain repository exposes reads and writes for that aggregate, including pivot attaches. `SearchCache` stays a repository and model-hook helper; attach-only writes invalidate it inside the repository.
- Ports for external systems stay in Application and are implemented in Infrastructure. Image storage goes through `TemporaryImageStorageInterface`.
- Health, readiness, OpenAPI, and the local admin token route are not domain use cases.